Ends what a page can ask of Chrome's bubbles in the core's windows as if the user had dismissed
it: a device chooser (WebHID, WebUSB, Web Serial, Web Bluetooth), the safety tip on a lookalike
domain, the File System Access prompt to restore a file's permission, the low-storage bubble, the
prompt to remote a cast tab's video, and the iOS promo after a saved password. Each anchors to a
BrowserView, which the core's windows don't have, and a device request dereferenced the null in
bubble_anchor_util and took the browser down (issue #1640). A device request goes to the core's
chooser instead (//browser_core/hooks.h, #1649), before fullscreen drops; without one, dropping
its controller settles it as a cancel, so the page gets the rejection a user's cancel gives it.

